[Music]  remembrance weekend is one of the most  significant moments of the year for the  royal family a time when they all gather  together but we now know the queen is  going to miss the british legion's  festival of remembrance at the royal  albert hall  a statement from the palace said that  following on from their recent advice  that the queen should rest for a few  days her majesty's doctors have advised  that she should continue to rest for at  least the next two weeks the doctors  have advised that her majesty can  continue to undertake light desk-based  duties during this time including some  virtual audiences but not to undertake  any official visits her majesty regrets  that this means she'll be unable to  attend the festival of remembrance on  saturday the 13th of november they  stressed it is still her firm intention  to be at the cenotaph on remembrance  sunday where in recent years prince  charles has placed the nation's wreath  on her behalf  she lived through the second world war  she saw her father lead the nation and  she served herself and for her  this is a prime duty of the monarch  she'll hate missing it but she'll try to  be ready for the remembrance sunday  service this was the queen's last public  outing a week and a half ago  since then she spent a night in hospital  after having preliminary tests we don't  know what for and canceled two major  engagements a trip to northern ireland  and her appearance at the climate summit  in glasgow  i understand that the queen has been  well enough to record a message that  will be played at cop 26 and again the  palace have used that phrase saying that  she is in good spirits they know that  people will understandably be concerned  about her she is after all 95 years old  but they want to stress that doctors are  being cautious and she is still working  away behind the scenes  this week she's welcomed two new  ambassadors to the uk  i'm very glad to have the chance to  see you if only mechanically this  morning  and presented her award for poetry the  queen no doubt also wanting to send a  subtle message of reassurance as she's  so often done during her reign  rhiannon mills sky news at windsor  castle

